# Stable addresses. The apps' update feeds and packages, the links in the
# apps and the Windows installer, the pages of this site and the Homebrew cask
# name only these; each leads to where the releases and the issue tracker are
# hosted now. Moving them changes these lines and a deploy of the site, never
# an installed app. 302, not 301, so no client keeps an old target.
#
#   /latest/<file>            that file of the newest release (update.json,
#                             update-windows.json)
#   /download/v<v>/<file>     that file of release v<v> (the packages)
#   /releases/v<v>            release v<v>'s page
#   /releases, /releases/latest, /issues
#
# scripts/publish-site.sh checks that every one is here and that all lead to
# the repository it names (REPO); scripts/release.sh publishes to the
# repository the /latest/* line names, and checks the deployed site leads
# there before it publishes anything.
/releases          https://github.com/tasict/Turnout/releases  302
/releases/latest   https://github.com/tasict/Turnout/releases/latest  302
/releases/*        https://github.com/tasict/Turnout/releases/tag/:splat  302
/latest/*          https://github.com/tasict/Turnout/releases/latest/download/:splat  302
/download/*        https://github.com/tasict/Turnout/releases/download/:splat  302
/issues            https://github.com/tasict/Turnout/issues  302
